ing unshown, making it the hardest to build around. T5 is also isolated but there's still 1 T5 unshown. However, T5 doesn't fit with my Character-heavy hand at all.\n\nBetween J2 and T5, I should discard **T5** because:\n- It's from a different suit than my core hand\n- Keeping J2 at least maintains honor tile options\n- This maintains maximum flexibility in the Character suit\n\nReason: My hand is strongly Character-suit oriented with W1(\u00d72), W2(\u00d72), and W4(\u00d73). The T5 is completely isolated from this structure and doesn't contribute to any viable winning pattern. Discarding T5 maintains my Character suit concentration while removing a tile that has minimal synergy with the rest of my hand.\n\nAnswer: Play T5"}
