ngs\"\n\nReason: I should **Pass** because: (1) Peng W1 would create three exposed melds, severely limiting my scoring potential and eliminating patterns like \"Concealed Hand\" (2 points) or \"Fully Concealed Hand\" (4 points); (2) My hand has W4 pung which is valuable to keep concealed; (3) The remaining tiles after Peng would be awkward to organize (W2, W2, W4, W4, W4, W5, F1, J2); (4) Keeping W1(2) allows flexibility for W1-W2-W3 chow formation with the 2 remaining W3 tiles; (5) With limited tiles left in the wall (many suits exhausted), I need maximum flexibility rather than committing to another exposed meld.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
