ally removes a potential pair option but creates a guaranteed meld. But the remaining tiles are too scattered.\n\nReason: \nPassing is the better choice because Peng W2 would leave me with an unworkable hand (W1, W1, W4, W4, W4, W5, F1, J2). These remaining 8 tiles cannot realistically form the required 1 meld + 1 pair due to isolation of W5, F1, and J2. By passing, I maintain flexibility to potentially draw useful tiles like W3 to form sequences, even though the overall hand structure remains challenging.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
